Start();
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking Utilities list;

/*  holderT -- .parenT THROUGH AN ACTION-ARGUMENT HOLDER. Minted 2026-09-01 as
    incant/fixits/parentUnreachable's COVERAGE HANDOFF when that citizen retired
    by ruling (SEQ 104, the fixit cull). The citizen is gone; this row is what
    remains of it, and it is the whole of what remains.

    THE DEFECT, measured 2026-08-29 and unchanged since: an action reaches its
    argument's PROPERTIES correctly through the holder and its argument's PARENT
    incorrectly. runAction binds by `ruleArg.group = argument`, so an action's
    `argument` is a FIELD POINTING AT the subject, not the subject. Property
    cases read through that; the node-returning case does not, and hands back
    the HOLDER, whose tag is `argument`.

    ⚠⚠ RE-PINNED 2026-09-02 TO htWindow, AND IT ARRIVED AT gNoUnwrap 0. The
    pin above predicted the FLIP would fix this and named the wrong cause. The
    trigger was setGroup's COPY: runAction binds `ruleArg.group = argument`, and
    the old setGroup copied a parented source and reparented the copy onto the
    holder, so .parenT read the holder. setGroup no longer copies, so .parenT
    reaches htWindow. The flip is still off and had nothing to do with it.

    ⚠ THE LESSON IS ABOUT PINS, NOT ABOUT PARENTS: a pin at a known-wrong value
    is worth keeping, and a pin's stated TRIGGER is a prediction that can be
    wrong on its own. This one held its value correctly for four days while
    naming the wrong cause the whole time, and nothing in the row could have
    caught that -- only the fix arriving from somewhere else did.

    ROWS 1 AND 2 ARE THE ANTI-VACUITY PAIR AND MUST BE GREEN ALWAYS. Row 1 is
    the same accessor read DIRECTLY, which is correct today and must stay
    correct -- without it, row 3 cannot tell "the holder loses the parent" from
    "the accessor is broken everywhere". Row 2 proves the node under test is the
    one intended; a walk that reads the wrong node agrees with itself.  */

register(HolderT);
define
    htWindow x=0 y=0 width=100 height=100
        htInside x=10 y=10 width=20 height=20;

    htDirect code={
        htKid <- htWindow["htInside"];
        print "holderT 2 identity  .taG    =" htKid.taG "  want htInside":;
        htU <- htKid.parenT;
        print "holderT 1 direct    .parenT =" htU.taG "  want htWindow":;
        };

    htProbe argument code={
        htP <- argument.parenT;
        print "holderT 3 holder    .parenT =" htP.taG "  want htWindow":;
        };

    htRun code={
        htDirect();
        htChild <- htWindow["htInside"];
        htProbe(htChild);
        };
    ;
htRun();
print "HOLDERT SENTINEL -- reached the foot":;
stop();
